# Blog Content Rules

## Pillar Page Internal Linking

Every color-analysis-related blog post MUST include a link to the Pillar Page in its "Related Articles" section:

```markdown
## Related Articles

- [Color Analysis: The Complete Guide](/en/color-analysis) — Everything you need to know about finding your best colors
```

A blog post is "color-analysis-related" if it covers ANY of these topics:
- Color analysis / seasonal color analysis / personal color analysis
- Color seasons (Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter and their 12 sub-seasons)
- Undertone, skin tone, color matching
- Makeup colors, wardrobe colors, hair colors by season
- Color quiz, draping, AI color analysis

## Sub-Season Palette Linking

If a blog post covers a specific season or sub-season, also link to its palette page:

```markdown
- [Light Spring Color Palette](/en/color-palette/light-spring) — Full palette guide for Light Spring
```

## Audience-Specific Linking

If a blog post covers a specific audience (e.g., men, dark skin, redheads), also link to the corresponding attribute page:

```markdown
- [Color Analysis for Men](/en/color-analysis-for/men) — Complete guide for men
```

## Checklist for New Blog Posts

1. Add the blog post markdown file to `src/content/blog/en/`
2. Add the Pillar Page link to the "Related Articles" section
3. Add relevant sub-season or attribute page links if applicable
4. Ensure the post is linked FROM the Pillar Page's "Further Reading" section if it's a key article (edit `src/app/[locale]/color-analysis/page.tsx`)
5. Update the sitemap if needed (usually automatic for blog posts)

## Language Tier Policy

Active locales (create new blog content for these): en, zh, ja, ko, es, de, pt, ru, tr, id

Demoted locales (DO NOT create new blog posts for these): ar, hi, th, vi

When creating a new blog post, only create translations for the 10 active locales above. Existing content in demoted locales should be left as-is.

Note: fr and it are borderline — they have some impressions but very low CTR. They remain active for now but are under review.
